      "id": 1,
      "text": "Mountain Brook was developed in 1929 by real‑estate businessman Robert Jemison Jr. as a suburb of Birmingham along Red Mountain and Shades Mountain.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain_Brook%2C_Alabama",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city’s name comes from a local Mountain Brook Store in Blount County, according to one account.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/mountain-brook/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Mountain Brook is home to the first office park in the U.S., built in 1955, featuring ample free parking and low‑profile buildings surrounded by landscaped grounds.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain_Brook%2C_Alabama",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The city’s streets were designed by landscape architect Warren H. Manning, who called for estate‑sized lots and three picturesque villages: English Village, Mountain Brook Village, and Crestline Village.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain_Brook%2C_Alabama",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Mountain Brook preserves 92.03% tree cover, one of the highest ratios in the nation, thanks to its forested residential sections like Cherokee Bend and Brookwood Forest.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain_Brook%2C_Alabama",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Actress Courteney Cox was born and raised in Mountain Brook, making the city the hometown of a Hollywood star.",
